+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: ratelimit
+status: draft
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, rate-limiting, token-bucket]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 0
+lane: light
+summary: "Token-bucket RateLimiter in timeparse/ratelimit.py with allow() and retry_after()"
+---
+
+# SPEC: ratelimit
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+Callers of `timeparse` have a duration parser but no way to throttle work by it. Add a small token-bucket limiter whose rate is written as `"N/DURATION"`, reusing `parse_duration`, so rates read like `"5/1m"`.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+A caller can build `RateLimiter("10/1s", burst=5)`, call `allow()` to gate work, and call `retry_after()` to learn how long to wait. Time is injectable via `clock`, so behavior is deterministic in tests.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: Construction and validation (AC-001)
+**Given** a `rate` string, a `burst`, and optionally a `clock`
+**When** `RateLimiter(rate, burst, clock)` is called
+**Then** `"10/1s"`, `"5/1m"`, `"3/1h30m"` with burst 1 or more are accepted
+**And** `ValueError` is raised for: no `/` or more than one `/`; `N` not a positive integer (`"0/1s"`, `"-1/1s"`, `"1.5/1s"`, `"/1s"`, non-digit); a `DURATION` that `parse_duration` rejects or that parses to 0 (`"5/0s"`, `"5/xyz"`); a non-string `rate`; a `burst` that is not a positive integer (0, negative, float, bool).
+
+### S2: Allow and continuous refill (AC-002)
+**Given** `rate="10/1s"`, `burst=1`, and a fake clock
+**When** `allow()` is called at clock readings 0.0, 0.1, 0.2, … 1.0
+**Then** every call returns `True`
+**And** a call at 0.05 after the call at 0.0 returns `False` and does not consume a token
+**And** the bucket starts full (`burst` consecutive `allow()` at one instant succeed, the next fails) and never holds more than `burst` tokens after a long idle.
+
+### S3: Multi-token takes are all-or-nothing (AC-003)
+**Given** `rate="1/1s"`, `burst=5`, 3 tokens available
+**When** `allow(4)` is called
+**Then** it returns `False` and the 3 tokens remain
+**And** `allow(3)` then returns `True`.
+
+### S4: retry_after (AC-004)
+**Given** `rate="10/1s"`, `burst=5`, bucket drained at t=0.0
+**When** `retry_after(n)` is called
+**Then** it returns `n/10` seconds at t=0.0, shrinks as the clock advances, and is `0.0` once `n` tokens are due
+**And** it is `0.0` on a full bucket, and calling it never takes tokens.
+
+### S5: n bounds (AC-005)
+**Given** any limiter with `burst=B`
+**When** `allow(n)` or `retry_after(n)` is called with `n < 1`, `n > B`, or a non-integer `n`
+**Then** `ValueError` is raised and no tokens are taken.
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Thread safety, async, or blocking/sleeping `wait()` helpers.
+- Per-key limiters, persistence, or shared state across processes.
+- Fractional rates (`N` is an integer) and an upper cap on `burst`; `burst` has no default and is required.
+- CLI exposure of the limiter.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | Existing `tests/` and `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` in pyproject.toml |
+| Default clock | `time.monotonic`, as in the request's signature | Stated in the request |
+| Dependencies | stdlib + `timeparse.parse.parse_duration` only | No new external dependency |
+| Float tolerance | A token counts as available when `tokens >= n - 1e-9` | S2's 0.1-step sequence: `0.3 - 0.2` is `0.0999…98`, so an exact compare would wrongly reject a token that is due |
+| Clock regression | A reading earlier than the last one adds no tokens (elapsed clamped to 0) | `time.monotonic` never regresses; this keeps a bad injected clock from minting tokens |
+| Compatibility | Python version of `pyproject.toml` | Existing package |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none — a new, additive, internal-to-package module; no schema, migration, permission boundary or dependency change. The public signature is new and cheap to revise before any release.
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_s1_construction_validation` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_s2_allow_refill_sequence` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_s3_multi_token_all_or_nothing` |
+| S4 | unit | `test_s4_retry_after` |
+| S5 | unit | `test_s5_n_bounds` |
+
+### AC-001: Construction and validation
+Oracle: golden. Evidence: valid and invalid cases are enumerated from the user's request, not derived from the implementation.
+
+### AC-002: Allow and continuous refill
+Oracle: golden. Evidence: the 0.0–1.0 sequence and the 0.05 rejection are stated in the request.
+
+### AC-003: Multi-token takes are all-or-nothing
+Oracle: property. Evidence: a rejected `allow(n)` leaves `retry_after` and later `allow` results identical to a run in which it was never called, whatever the implementation.
+
+### AC-004: retry_after
+Oracle: golden. Evidence: `n/10` at t=0 follows from the stated rate; consistency check: advancing the clock by `retry_after(n)` makes `allow(n)` return `True`.
+
+### AC-005: n bounds
+Oracle: golden. Evidence: bounds 1..burst are stated in the request.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+- Is `RateLimiter` exported from `timeparse/__init__.py` (public API contract, which may be irreversible) or reachable only as `timeparse.ratelimit.RateLimiter`? Default until answered: not exported; `/hm:execute` Step 0 resolves it. If exported, add an `IRR-001` and re-run as `full`.
+- Whitespace/case handling of `N` and the slash (`"10 / 1s"`): default is strict — only `parse_duration`'s own trimming applies to the DURATION part; `N` must be bare ASCII digits.
+
+## 🔎 Spec Validation
+spec-validator: MAJOR_REVISION (advisory). Findings, one pass:
+- critical: AC-002 golden table has only `True` rows, so an `allow()` that never limits would pass. Execute must author the test from S2 prose as a stateful sequence: 0.05 rejection, burst+1th failure, idle cap, non-consumption.
+- AC-001, AC-004, AC-005 machine tables are thinner than S1/S4/S5. Execute must cover every S1 invalid class (including `"5/1s/2s"`, bool/float `burst`, non-string rate), a mid-drain and exact-due `retry_after`, and `n` of float/bool/str type on both methods with state unchanged.
+- warning: public API contract not listed as irreversible. Recorded above as an open question.
+- Circular oracles: none found.
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Lane `light`: one new module plus one test file, one session, no irreversible decision. Interview skipped as the request already fixes the contract; autopilot is `auto_full`, so the DRI was not asked.
+- Defaulted (not asked): float tolerance 1e-9, clamp of regressing clocks, rejection of bool/float for `N`, `burst`, `n`, and zero-length durations.
+- Autopilot `auto_full` auto-answered the pending judgment gate (open questions on export location and `N` whitespace). No approval was written; the SPEC stays unaccepted at `status: draft`, with the defaults above standing until `/hm:execute` Step 0 resolves them.
