+spec_need_target: ratelimit
+---
+
+## 🎯 Executive Summary
+Add `RateLimiter(rate, burst, clock)` with `allow(n)` and `retry_after(n)` as a new module, covering SPEC S1-S5 (AC-001..AC-005). Decisions below are the reversible calls the SPEC left open.
+
+## 📚 Prior Work
+No prior PLANs or SPECs. `parse_duration` in `timeparse/parse.py` returns int seconds and raises `ValueError`; reused for the DURATION part.
+
+## 📐 Architecture Decision Records
+- ADR-001: Track tokens as a float plus the last clock reading; refill lazily on each call as `min(burst, tokens + elapsed * rate_per_sec)`. **Decided by:** agent
+- ADR-002: A token is available when `tokens >= n - 1e-9`; `retry_after` is `max(0.0, (n - tokens) / rate_per_sec)`, and `0.0` when within that tolerance. **Decided by:** user (source: SPEC Constraints, float tolerance and S2 sequence)
+- ADR-003: `RateLimiter` is not exported from `timeparse/__init__.py` (SPEC open question, default). Consumers import `timeparse.ratelimit`. **Decided by:** agent
+- ADR-004: Strict validation: `rate` must be `str` with exactly one `/`; `N` is ASCII digits only and positive; `burst` and `n` are `int` but not `bool`. **Decided by:** agent
+
+## 🏗️ Technical Design
+New `timeparse/ratelimit.py` imports `parse_duration` from `timeparse.parse`. State: `_rate` (tokens/sec), `_burst`, `_clock`, `_tokens` (starts at burst), `_last` (clock reading at construction). A regressing clock gives elapsed 0. Validation of `n` precedes any state change; a failed `allow` mutates nothing except the refill, which is idempotent.
+
+## 📝 Implementation Plan
+- [x] 1. **Phase 1 — tests and RateLimiter** — depends_on: none · parallel_group: none · merge_hazards: none · scope: in `tests/test_ratelimit.py`, `timeparse/ratelimit.py`; out: every other file · exit: `uv run pytest -q` · risk: low · rollback: delete the two new files
+
+## 🚧 Contract Boundaries
+### Do not change
+- `timeparse/parse.py` — parse_duration behavior is relied on, not modified
+- `timeparse/__init__.py` — export decision deferred (ADR-003)
+
+## 🧪 Testing Strategy
+pytest unit tests, one per scenario: `test_s1_construction_validation`, `test_s2_allow_refill_sequence`, `test_s3_multi_token_all_or_nothing`, `test_s4_retry_after`, `test_s5_n_bounds`. A fake clock is injected. Hypothesis is not installed here, so the AC-003 property is checked as a two-run comparison over a fixed set of cases.
+
+## ⚠️ Risks & Mitigation
+| Risk | Mitigation |
+|---|---|
+| Float error rejects a due token | ADR-002 tolerance, tested on the 0.1-step sequence |
+| Tests derived from the code | Expected values taken from the SPEC golden tables |
+
+## ✅ Success Criteria
+- [x] S1-S5 tests pass
+- [x] full suite green (`python -m pytest -q`: 78 passed)
